            "subject": "LU-20867 gss: re-resolve lsvcgssd ioctl device on failure"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Patrick Farrell",
          "email": "patrick@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-29 21:27:22.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-29 21:27:22.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity test_398m",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity test_398m\n\nThe test checks that parallel DIO reports an error when an OST\nfails the bulk RPC. With the fail_loc set, every bulk RPC\nreturns -EIO and the client resends 10 times (resend_count)\nwith a growing backoff, so each of the four expected-failure\ndd runs takes close to a minute.\n\nSet osc.*.resend_count to 1 for the test and restore it with\nstack_trap, as sanity 77f does. The dd runs still fail with the\nerror, only the retry backoff is gone.\n\nOn a VM the test took 75s, 45s and 65s before and 8s, 7s and\n6s after. CI averages 235s over 17259 runs per 30 days; saving\nabout 220s per run is about 1050 hours per 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=398m\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I76c76c266f66a10d5f43e776bc7e979072ca738d\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
